  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I found TX-0401 in account ACC-1005 and verified its amount:\n\n- **Amount:** EUR 240.00 (outgoing card payment)\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Status:** Settled\n\nYour account also shows **TX-0402**, a second EUR 240.00 card payment to TechMart Online on 2026-07-14, also settled. The two charges have the same amount and merchant.\n\nBased on the records, these reason codes could apply, depending on what happened:\n\n1. **duplicate_charge:** This fits if you intended to pay TechMart only once. The matching TX-0402 would be the likely duplicate.\n2. **unauthorized_debit:** This fits if you did not make or approve this payment.\n3. **fraud_card_not_present:** This fits if the card was used online without your authorization, which is consistent with a card payment to an online merchant.\n4. **goods_not_received:** This fits if you paid for an item or order that was never delivered.\n5. **service_not_rendered:** This fits if you paid for a service that was not provided.\n\nIf you tell me which of these matches your situation, I can check whether TX-0401 is eligible for a dispute under that reason code before anything is filed. I will not open a dispute without your confirmation.",
